Sorry I don't follow. Why would following method not work and require using `INSTANCE`?
```
public void writeTo(StreamOutput out) {
  out.writeBoolean(true);
  out.writeString(SystemUser.NAME);
}
```

We'd have to use it here:

https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/master/x-pack/plugin/core/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/core/security/authc/Authentication.java#L978-L979

i.e., 

```
if (SystemUser.is(user)) {
    SystemUser.INSTANCE.writeTo(output);
}
```

But `INSTANCE` is a `User` and does not expose `writeTo`; don't think it necessarily makes sense to change `INSTANCE` class from `User` to `SystemUser`

